The version of the JQuery library we use for the https://git-lfs.com home page was released in 2016 and is the subject of a few security reports, so although our use of JQuery is limited, we update it to the latest version.  We also simplify our JavaScript code which performs a basic attempt at client OS detection.

First, we update our version of JQuery from is 1.12.4 to 3.7.1.  The older version is the subject of a number of security issues, including:

- CVE-2019-11358
- CVE-2020-11022
- CVE-2020-23064

Next, we remove our use of the `session.min.js` JavaScript library, which appears to be from the `codejoust/session.js` [project](https://github.com/codejoust/session.js).  Our version seems to match the code in the `session.js` [file](https://github.com/codejoust/session.js/blob/80b25af34551443ac77b45c26a798b2c52a4a209/session.js) following PR codejoust/session.js#41, with minification applied manually.  Regardless, as that project has not received updates in the last four years, and we only use a very small fraction of its functionality, we replace it with a few lines of CoffeeScript to perform a basic form of OS detection using the same technique as the `codejoust/session.js` library, namely a search for the specific strings `Mac` or `Linux` in the `navigator.platform` variable.

This variable's use is deprecated in current MDN JavaScript [documentation](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Navigator/platform); however, it remains the most straightforward
way of performing the basic and limited OS detection we require.  In future we may choose to replace this with another approach, such as the [User-Agent Client Hints API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/User-Agent_Client_Hints_API), but this is [not yet supported](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WorkerNavigator/userAgentData) by some major Web clients such as Firefox at the present time.

Both the legacy version of the `codejoust/session.js` library and the most recent update to that library (from 2019) [pass](https://github.com/codejoust/session.js/blob/1bb9844ae83209907c8f33704771345f496c3396/session.js#L592) the `navigator` object to the library's `session_fetch()` function, which [calls](https://github.com/codejoust/session.js/blob/1bb9844ae83209907c8f33704771345f496c3396/session.js#L150) the library's`search()` function to set the `os` variable we [check](https://github.com/git-lfs/git-lfs.github.com/blob/08debbed6d7bd4d4185c4711cfcbee9fa2a552d0/js/_scripts/main.coffee#L2), passing an internal `data.os` [array](https://github.com/codejoust/session.js/blob/1bb9844ae83209907c8f33704771345f496c3396/session.js#L202-L209) containing the possible OS types and their identifying strings.  The `search()` function then [tests](https://github.com/codejoust/session.js/blob/1bb9844ae83209907c8f33704771345f496c3396/session.js#L166-L177) for a match with one of these array elements, and in the case of the two [checks](https://github.com/git-lfs/git-lfs.github.com/blob/08debbed6d7bd4d4185c4711cfcbee9fa2a552d0/js/_scripts/main.coffee#L3-L6) we perform (for MacOS and Linux) this is just a [search](https://github.com/codejoust/session.js/blob/1bb9844ae83209907c8f33704771345f496c3396/session.js#L171) for a given substring (`Mac` or `Linux`) in the string returned by `navigator.platform`.

Thus we can just perform these simple checks ourselves, which will suffice for our purposes, and avoid the need to use a legacy JS library entirely.  Our replacement CoffeeScript compiles to the following JavaScript:

```javascript
$(function() {
    var platform;
    platform = window.navigator.platform;
    if ((platform.indexOf('Mac')) !== -1) {
        return $('.js-mac').removeClass('visually-hidden');
    } else if ((platform.indexOf('Linux')) !== -1) {
        return $('.js-linux').removeClass('visually-hidden');
    } else {
        return $('.js-windows').removeClass('visually-hidden');
    }
});
```

Finally, we can adjust the file permissions on one static file to remove its unnecessary executable file permissions.

This PR now addresses REG-1342, which is all about supporting validations, screenshots, and replay data for local bots.
You can try this out in BossRoom by doing the following:

* Pulling this branch
* Pull the backend code from here, and restart RGService - https://github.com/Regression-Games/RegressionGames/pull/430
* Make a local bot from the code at the end of this description, and then sync your bots.

Once you run your bot in bossroom, you should be able to go to the bot history page and open validations! Make sure your client is up to date as well.

Tasks remaining for this ticket:

* Review the threading and async approach and fix any issues you think may be there
* There is a bug with replay data - I _think_ the format I am saving is valid, but the replay data pane won't load the zip, due to the RGEntity interface - we should verify that remote replay data still works

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using RegressionGames;
using RegressionGames.RGBotLocalRuntime;
using RegressionGames.StateActionTypes;
using UnityEngine;

namespace AbilityBot_0
{
    public class BotEntryPoint : RGUserBot
    {

        protected override bool GetIsSpawnable()
        {
            return true;
        }

        protected override RGBotLifecycle GetBotLifecycle()
        {
            return RGBotLifecycle.MANAGED;
        }

        public override void ConfigureBot(RG rgObject)
        {
            var classIndex = new System.Random().Next(4);
            var classes = new string[] {"Mage", "Rogue", "Tank", "Archer"};
            rgObject.CharacterConfig = new Dictionary<string, object>() {
                { "characterType", $"{classes[classIndex]}" }
            };
        }

        public override void ProcessTick(RG rgObject)
        {
            try
            {
                var entities = rgObject.FindEntities();
                if (entities.Count > 0)
                {
                    // default to friendly ability
                    var skillId = 0;
                    var target = entities[new System.Random().Next(entities.Count)];
                    if (target.GetField<int>("team", 0) == 1)
                    {
                        // if enemy.. set ability to 1
                        skillId = 1;
                    }

                    rgObject.RecordValidation("Test passed", RGValidationResultType.PASS, "heart");
                    rgObject.RecordValidation("Test failed", RGValidationResultType.FAIL, "heart");
                    rgObject.RecordValidation("Test warning", RGValidationResultType.WARNING, "heart");

                    var targetPosition = target.position;
                    var action = new RGActionRequest("PerformSkill", new Dictionary<string, object>()
                    {
                        { "skillId",  skillId},
                        { "targetId", target["id"] },
                        { "xPosition", targetPosition.x },
                        { "yPosition", targetPosition.y },
                        { "zPosition", targetPosition.z },
                    });
                    rgObject.PerformAction(action);
                }
                else
                {
                    RGDebug.LogWarning("No entities found...");
                }
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                RGDebug.LogError($"Error getting target position: {ex}");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

